A callee whose answer is a case writes the cell on one arm and moves its contents to another field on another; a run goes through one arm, and the caller reads the call as a case of the callee's paths. Each write is accepted and runs in place (ownership-v3-kernel.md §13 item 13). A helper whose arm moves the first part of a pair to the second is called before the arm that writes the first. Its live twin is CellCalleePathsLive.
